#: ../../source/templates_miro.md:16
msgid "1. Visual Theme & Atmosphere"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_miro.md:18
msgid ""
"Miro's website is a clean, collaborative-tool-forward platform that "
"communicates \"visual thinking\" through generous whitespace, pastel "
"accent colors, and a confident geometric font. The design uses a "
"predominantly white canvas with near-black text (`#1c1c1e`) and a "
"distinctive pastel color palette — coral, rose, teal, orange, yellow, "
"moss — each representing different collaboration contexts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/templates_miro.md:20
msgid ""
"The typography uses Roobert PRO Medium as the primary display font with "
"OpenType character variants (`\"blwf\", \"cv03\", \"cv04\", \"cv09\", "
"\"cv11\"`) and negative letter-spacing (-1.68px at 56px). Noto Sans "
"handles body text with its own stylistic set (`\"liga\" 0, \"ss01\", "
"\"ss04\", \"ss05\"`). The design is built with Framer, giving it smooth "
"animations and modern component patterns."
msgstr ""

